      "description": "`a` has a null in the middle. A stacked ribbon has no way to draw a hole, so the null becomes `0` and the band pinches shut instead of breaking. **An outage therefore looks exactly like a legitimate zero.** This is the one contract rule that differs sharply from the cartesian families (where a null stays a gap), and there is no code workaround — ECharts cannot break a ribbon.",
